  "body": "## Overview\n\nFixes #29388.\n\nFor embedding and reranking models whose compute graph never outputs logits, `output_reserve()` still allocated and zero-filled an `n_vocab * n_outputs` float buffer. For large vocabularies (bge-m3: 250002, EmbeddingGemma: 262144), this wastes roughly 1 MiB host RAM per token. As reported in #29388, at default server concurrency (4 slots sharing up to `n_ubatch` tokens), this caused EmbeddingGemma to get OOM-killed in a 2.6 GB cgroup.\n\nThe logits buffer is now kept when embeddings are off, and skipped only when embeddings are on and the reserve graph has no logits tensor.\n\nAPI change: for models without logits, `llama_get_logits()` returns `NULL` instead of a zero-filled buffer. `llama_get_logits_ith()`  logs an error and triggers  `GGML_ABORT` in Debug builds.\n\n## Additional information\n\nRelated:\n1.) #29576 touches the same function (sampling buffers) and merges without conflict.\n2.) #25964 adds an opt-in flag to skip LM-head compute.\n\n### Memory growth over idle (Q8_0 GGUFs)\n\n`llama-server --embeddings -ub 2048 -b 2048 -np 1 -c 8192 -t 8`\n\n**CPU (`RssAnon` from `/proc/<pid>/status`):**\n\n| Model (vocab) | Prompt tokens (min / max) | master (79e2e74eb) | patched |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| bge-m3 (250002) | 26 / 1952 | +26 MB / +1939 MB | +1 MB / +81 MB (~1.85 GB saved) |\n| EmbeddingGemma-300M (262144) | 18 / 1302 | +19 MB / +1353 MB | +1 MB / +49 MB (~1.3 GB saved) |\n| nomic-embed-text-v1.5 (30522) | 18 / 1302 | +5 MB / +238 MB | +3 MB / +77 MB |\n| bge-reranker-v2-m3 (rank pooling) | 29 / 1955 | +29 MB / +1943 MB | +1 MB / +81 MB |\n\n**CUDA (`VmRSS` / `RssShmem`, `-ngl 99`):**\n\nOn CUDA, the pinned host buffer is accounted for under `RssShmem` rather than `RssAnon`, so `VmRSS` reflects the saving (single request per model):\n\n| Model | Prompt tokens | master (79e2e74eb) | patched |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| bge-m3 | 1952 | +1878 MB | +17 MB |\n| EmbeddingGemma-300M | 1302 | +1315 MB | +13 MB |\n| nomic-embed-text-v1.5 | 1302 | +166 MB | +14 MB |\n\n(VRAM usage is unchanged at ~490 MiB on both; the saving is host RAM).\n\n### Testing\n\nTested on CPU (Intel Xeon Platinum, 8 threads, aws instance: g4dn.2xlarge) and CUDA (Tesla T4, CUDA 13.3, `-ngl 99`). Other backends (Metal, Vulkan, etc.) are untested.\n\n- Parity checks:\n  - CPU: embeddings, rerank scores, text generation (stories260K, LFM2, flan-t5-small), and perplexity are bit-identical to master.\n  - CUDA: embeddings and rerank scores are identical across all four models; server completions plus embeddings are identical on stories260K and LFM2.\n- LFM2 toggle: logits are restored when dynamically switching `llama_set_embeddings()` off (verified on CPU and CUDA).\n\n## Requirements\n\n- I have read and agree with the [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- AI usage disclosure: YES, used ByteAsk agent (with Sonnet)  for A/B benchmark scripts and /proc memory logging. Code changes are minimal and all done by me; results verified by me.\n",
